# 4. REQUIRED FRONTEND ARCHITECTURE

Build a real shared dossier presentation foundation.

Inspect current Feature-Sliced Design architecture before choosing file locations.

Prefer an appropriate shared entity/widget composition.

Suggested conceptual architecture:

```text
Shared Application Dossier Presentation
│
├── Dossier Header
├── Five-Criterion Navigation
├── Criterion Details
│   ├── Requirement Groups
│   ├── Student Declaration Cards
│   └── Evidence Cards / Viewer
├── Applicable Regulations
└── Dossier Navigation / Anchors
```

These are the shared presentation capabilities.

Role-specific actions must be composed separately:

```text
Student Dossier
  └── Shared Dossier + Student editing actions

School Officer Dossier
  └── Shared Dossier + School preliminary review actions

City Officer Dossier
  └── Shared Dossier + Assigned City review actions

Committee Dossier
  └── Shared Dossier + Committee authorized controls
```

Do not make shared presentation components import an entire role-specific feature module.

Respect FSD dependency direction.

Avoid circular imports.

Do not create one gigantic component containing all four role implementations.

Use composition and small, cohesive role-specific components.

