# 6. ROLE-BASED PRESENTATION MODES

Use a strongly typed capabilities model consistent with the existing authorization architecture.

Suggested conceptual modes:

```typescript
type DossierPresentationMode =
  | "student_edit"
  | "student_readonly"
  | "school_review"
  | "city_review"
  | "committee_review";
```

Adapt to existing canonical conventions.

This type is illustrative, not a mandate to duplicate already existing models.

## Important

The presentation mode controls UI composition only.

It is not a replacement for backend RBAC or ABAC.

The server must remain authoritative for every read and write operation.

Do not assume a frontend role string grants actual permission.

Do not hardcode access based only on the existence of a button.

