# 14. CRITERION AND DECLARATION REVIEW UX

Reviewers should be able to inspect information quickly.

Suggested behavior:

1. Select criterion.
2. See the existing Student declaration layout.
3. Expand the relevant declaration.
4. Open linked evidence.
5. Inspect the applicable requirement.
6. Record authorized judgment.
7. Continue to the next relevant item.

Avoid creating a separate multi-step wizard for normal review.

## Preserve existing review semantics

If the system records judgments at declaration, evidence, requirement or criterion level, keep those existing domain semantics.

Do not silently replace them with a single criterion-level PASS button if the backend requires more granular recorded decisions.

Likewise, do not introduce more granular review actions merely to make the UI appear sophisticated.

Use the actual authorized backend workflow.

## Supplementation

The existing scoped supplementation capability must remain functional.

Do not add the removed ambiguous-case process back under another name.

